hadiths[73]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2434","[AI-translation] Narrated Husain bin Ali, relating that the Prophet, peace be upon him, hid for Ibn Sayyad (smoke). He asked him about what he had hidden for him. He said: ""Dukh."" He said: ""Away with you! You will not exceed your measure."" When he turned away, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""What did he say?"" Some of them said: ""Dukh."" And some of them said: ""Rather, he said: Zukh."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""You have differed while I am among you, and after me you will differ more severely."
"2435","[AI-translation] Narrated Samurah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""If I narrate a hadith to you, do not add to it."" And he said: ""Four are from the sweetest of speech, and they are from the Quran; it will not harm you with whichever of them you begin: Subhan Allah, Al-Hamdu Lillah, La ilaha illa Allah, and Allahu Akbar."" Then he said: ""Do not name your boy Aflah, nor Najih, nor Rabah, nor Yasar (for you will say: 'Is he there?' but he is not, so he will say: 'No')."
"2436","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Humaid or Abu Usaid who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When you hear a hadith from me which your hearts recognize, and your hair and skin soften to it, and you see it as close to you, then I am the most entitled to it. And when you hear a hadith from me which your hearts reject, and your hair and skin recoil from it, and you see it as far from you, then I am the farthest of you from it."
"2437","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: I left Al-Sham for Al-Madinah on Friday, so I entered upon Umar bin Al-Khattab. He said: ""When did you put your two socks on your feet?"" I said: ""On Friday."" He said: ""Did you take them off?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""You have hit the Sunnah."
"2438","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""I saw in a dream last night a canopy dripping with ghee and honey, and I saw people scooping from it—some taking much, some taking little. And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven. I saw you grasp it and ascend; then another man grasped it and ascended; then another man grasped it and ascended; then another man grasped it and it was severed, then it was rejoined for him and he ascended.""Abū Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be ransomed for you—allow me to interpret it."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Interpret it."" He said: ""As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for that which drips of honey and ghee, it is the Qurʾān—its sweetness drips—so the one who takes much of the Qurʾān and the one who takes little. As for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth, it is the Truth upon which you are; you grasp it and Allah raises you, then a man grasps it and rises, then another man grasps it and rises, then another man grasps it and it is severed for him, then it is rejoined for him and he rises."" He said: ""Inform me, O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be ransomed for you—did I get it right or err?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You got some right and you erred in some."" He said: ""By Allah, you must tell me what I erred in."" He said: ""Do not swear."""
"2439","[AI-translation] [He] said, peace be upon him: ""Most of the hypocrites of my Ummah are its reciters."" (This is reported from the hadith of Ubaidullah bin Amr, Uqbah bin Amir, Abdullah bin Abbas, and Asmah bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with them)."
"2440","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, commanded them, he would command them of the deeds that they were capable of. They said: ""We are not like you, O Messenger of Allah! Has Allah not forgiven for you what preceded of your sin and what was delayed?!"" He would become angry until anger was recognized in his face, then he would say: ""I am the most God-fearing of you and the most knowledgeable of Allah among you."
"2441","[AI-translation] Nahdi who said: I was with Umar while he was addressing the people, and he said in his sermon, mentioning it as marfu'an: ""The thing I fear most for my Ummah is every hypocrite with a knowing tongue."
"2442","[AI-translation] From Talhah ibn Musarrif, raised: ""Indeed, the thing I fear most for my Ummah in the end of time is three: belief in the stars, denial of Qadar, and the tyranny of the Sultan."
"2443","[AI-translation] From 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Indeed, the greatest of the Muslims (among the Muslims) in crime is he who asks about a thing that was not forbidden (and pried into it), so it was forbidden (upon the people) because of his question."
"2444","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Indeed, the one who lies upon me, a house will be built for him in the Fire."
"2445","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu': ""Indeed, Allah has withheld repentance from the companion of every innovation."
"2446","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, narrating, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: ""Indeed, the affair of this Ummah will not cease to be moderate or agreeable until they speak concerning children and Qadar."
"2447","[AI-translation] From Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: ""Indeed, when the Children of Israel perished, they narrated stories."
"2448","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""Indeed, Islam has a fervor, and every fervor has a slackening. So if its companion is upright and moderate, then hope for him; and if he is pointed to with the fingers, then do not hope for him."
"2449","[AI-translation] From Hiram ibn Hakim, from his uncle 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: ""(Indeed, you) are in a time in which its jurists are many, its preachers are few, its questioners are few, and its givers are many; action in it is better than knowledge. And there will come a time in which its jurists are few, its preachers are many, its questioners are many, and its givers are few; knowledge in it is better than action."
"2450","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""Indeed, knowledge is only attained through learning, and forbearance is only attained through enduring. Whoever seeks out good is given it, and whoever guards against evil is protected from it."
"2451","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu': ""The likeness of the companion of the Qur'an is only as the likeness of the owner of tethered camels; if he watches over them he retains them, and if he lets them loose they go away."
"2452","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah bin Amr who said: I set out for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) one day. He said: He heard the voices of two men disputing over a verse, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came out to us, anger recognizable on his face, and said: ""Those before you were only destroyed by their differing in the Book."
"2453","Abdur-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah said: I entered the mosque and found Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah with people gathered around him. I came to them and sat with him, and he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, so we stopped at a place. Some of us were fixing their tents, some were shooting arrows, and some were in their resting places when the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: ""Prayer is gathering!"" So we gathered to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ""There was no prophet before me except that it was incumbent upon him to guide his nation to the best of what he knows for them and warn them of the worst of what he knows for them. And your nation, its well-being was placed in its first part, and its last part will be afflicted with tribulations and matters you will deny. And a trial will come, making some of them follow others. And a trial will come, and the believer will say: 'This is my destruction!' Then it will be uncovered. And a trial will come, and the believer will say: 'This is it, this is it!' So whoever loves to be removed from the Fire and entered into Paradise, let his death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people the way he loves to be treated. And whoever pledges allegiance to an imam, giving him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as long as he is able. If another comes disputing with him, then strike the neck of the other.""And he added at the end: So I drew near to him and said: ""I adjure you by Allah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" So he pointed to his ears and his heart with his hands and said: ""My ears heard it and my heart preserved it."" I said to him: ""This is your cousin Mu'awiyah ordering us to consume our wealth among ourselves unjustly and kill ourselves, while Allah says: 'O you who have believed, do not consume one another's wealth unjustly but only [in lawful] business by mutual consent. And do not kill yourselves. Indeed Allah is to you ever Merciful.' (An-Nisa 4:29)"" He remained silent for a while, then said: ""Obey him in obedience to Allah, and disobey him in disobedience to Allah."""
"2454","On the authority of Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, while we were sitting on a mat: ""There will be a fitnah (trial/tribulation)."" They said: ""How should we act, O Messenger of Allah?"" He placed his hand back on the mat and grasped it, saying: ""You act like this."" And he mentioned to them one day: ""There will be a fitnah,"" but many people did not hear it. So Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: ""Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) says?"" They said: ""What did he say?"" He said: ""There will be a fitnah."" They said: ""How should we act, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""You return to your original state."""
"2455","On the authority of Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, while we were sitting on a mat: ""There will be a trial."" They said: ""How should we act, O Messenger of Allah?"" He placed his hand back on the mat and grasped it, saying: ""You act like this."" And he mentioned to them one day: ""There will be a trial,"" but many people did not hear it. So Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: ""Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) says?"" They said: ""What did he say?"" He said: ""There will be a trial."" They said: ""How should we act, O Messenger of Allah? Or what should we do?"" He said: ""You return to your original state."""
"2456","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""I return to my family and find a date fallen on my bed, so I pick it up to eat it, but then I fear it might be charity, so I cast it away."
"2457","[AI-translation] Miqdam bin Ma'di Karib al-Kindi, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""I was given the Book and what is equal to it (meaning: and its like). It is almost time for a satiated man reclining on his couch to say: 'Between us and you is this Book; whatever is lawful in it, we have made lawful, and whatever is unlawful in it, we have made unlawful.' Nay, it is not so! Lo! The predatory beast with fangs is not lawful, nor the domestic donkey, nor the found property of a covenanted person except if one has no need for it. And any man who is a guest of a people and they do not honor him, he may retaliate against them with the like of his hospitality."
"2458","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Qatadah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Beware of narrating much from me. Whoever attributes something to me, let him only say the truth. Whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2459","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a man standing in prayer upon a rock. He went to the side of Makkah and stayed a long while, then returned and found the man in his same state, praying. He clasped his hands together and said: ""O people, adhere to moderation, for Allah does not grow weary until you grow weary."
"2460","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""My Ummah will come to me at the Hawd, and I will drive the people away from it just as a man drives away the camels of another man from his own camels."" They said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Will you recognize us?"" He said: ""Yes, you will have a mark that no one other than you will have: you will come to me with radiant marks from the traces of ablution. A group of you will surely be turned away from me and will not reach me, so I will say: 'O Lord! These are my companions!' An angel will respond to me and say: 'Do you know what they did after you?'"
"2461","[AI-translation] Narrated from Kharijah bin Zayd from his father who said: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) arrived in Madinah, I was brought to him and I read to him. He said to me: ""Learn the writing of the Jews, for I do not trust them with our Book."" He said: So no more than fifteen days passed before I learned it, and I would write for the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and read their writings to him."
"2462","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Learn from your lineages what will enable you to maintain ties of kinship, for maintaining ties of kinship brings love among family, increase in wealth, and prolongation in lifespan."
"2463","[AI-translation] Khudri that he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Learn the Quran and ask Allah for Paradise by it before a people learn it and ask for the worldly life by it. For the Quran is learned by three: a man who boasts with it, a man who earns a living by it, and a man who reads it for the sake of Allah."
"2464","Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in that, for there were wonders among them."" Then he began to narrate and said: ""A group from the Children of Israel went out until they came to one of their graveyards. They said: 'Let us pray two rak'ahs and supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that He brings out for us a man from among those who have died, so we may ask him about death.' He said: So they did that. While they were in that state, a man peered his head out from a grave among those graves. He was dark-skinned, with the mark of prostration between his eyes. He said: 'O you people, what do you want from me? I have been dead for a hundred years, and the heat of death has not subsided from me until now. So supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for me that He returns me as I was.'"""
"2465","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah who said: A group of desert dwellers came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The people of the Quran claimed that no deed is of benefit without migration and jihad in the path of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Wherever you are, if you excel in the worship of Allah, then give glad tidings of Paradise."
"2466","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, marfu': All of creation invokes blessings upon the teacher of good, even the fish in the sea."
"2467","[AI-translation] From Yunus bin Maysarah bin Halbas who narrated saying: I heard Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan narrating from the Messenger of Allah: Goodness is a habit, and evil is obstinacy, and whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"2468","[AI-translation] He said: The one who guides to good is like its doer. It is reported from the hadith of Abu Mas'ud."
"2469","[AI-translation] From Jabir, marfu': Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."
"2470","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud, that he asked Ubayy bin Ka'b, while the Prophet of Allah was delivering the sermon, about a verse from the Book of Allah. He turned away from him and did not reply to him. When he finished his prayer, he said: You did not combine. So Ibn Mas'ud asked the Messenger of Allah, and he said: Ubayy spoke the truth."
"2471","[AI-translation] 'As who said: The Messenger of Allah said one day while we were sitting: Glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: And who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Righteous people, few among many evil people; those who disobey them are more than those who obey them."
"2472","On the authority of Ibn al-Adra', who said: I was guarding the Prophet ﷺ one night when he went out to relieve himself. He saw me, took my hand, and we walked on. We passed by a man praying and reciting the Qur'an aloud. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Perhaps he is showing off."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, he is reciting the Qur'an aloud."" He withdrew his hand and said: ""You will not attain this matter by force."" Then on another night, he went out while I was guarding him to relieve himself. He took my hand and we passed by a man praying with the Qur'an. I said: ""Perhaps he is showing off."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""No, indeed he is one who turns to Allah often in repentance."" I looked, and behold, it was Abdullah Dhu al-Najadayn."
"2473","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': Teach and make things easy, do not make things difficult; give glad tidings and do not repel; and if one of you becomes angry, let him remain silent."
"2474","On the authority of Al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave us an admonition that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble with fear. So we said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This is indeed the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?"" He said: ""I have left you upon the clear path, its night like its day; no one deviates from it after me except one who is doomed. And whoever among you lives long will see much difference. So hold fast to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me; cling to it with your molar teeth. And adhere to obedience, even if it be to an Abyssinian slave. For the believer is like a submissive camel; wherever it is led, it follows."""
"2475","[AI-translation] He said: Tie down knowledge by writing. It is reported from the hadith of Anas bin Malik, and 'Abd Allah bin 'Amr, and 'Abd Allah bin 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2476","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah who said: Whenever he found a report dubious, he would quote the verse of Tarafah: ""And he brings you news from one whom you did not provision."
"2477","[AI-translation] Ghazal from his father from his grandfather: Whenever he ascended the pulpit, we would turn our faces toward him."
"2478","[AI-translation] Narrated Jābir: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), whenever he ascended the minbar, would offer salām."
"2479","[AI-translation] Khudrī: He said, ""Welcome to the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to enjoin us regarding you."" Meaning: the seekers of Hadīth."
"2480","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Ā'ishah: His speech (peace be upon him and his family) was distinct speech, understood by everyone who heard it."
"2481","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to be pleased by a good dream."
"2482","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, benefit me by what You have taught me, teach me what will benefit me, and provide me with knowledge through which You benefit me."
"2483","[AI-translation] Narrated Abū Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is a sufficient sin for a man to relate everything he hears."
"2484","[AI-translation] Narrated Abū Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""All of my Ummah will enter Paradise except those who refuse."" It was said: ""And who would refuse?!"" He said: ""Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused."
"2485","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: There were two brothers during the time of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family). One of them used to come to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) (and in a narration: he would attend the discourse of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and his assembly) and the other would earn a living. The earner complained about his brother to the Prophet (peace be upon him) (and he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! ('Indeed, this') brother of mine does not help me with anything""), so he (peace be upon him) said: ""Perhaps you are provided for through him."
"2486","[AI-translation] Narrated Ubayy ibn Ka'b: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Which verse in the Book of Allah is the greatest?"" He said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He repeated it several times, then Ubayy said: ""The Verse of the Kursī."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""May knowledge rejoice you, O Abā al-Mundhir! By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, it possesses a tongue and two lips that glorify the King at the foot of the Throne."
"2487","[AI-translation] Narrated Abū Hurayrah (mawqūf): Milk in a dream is fiṭrah."
"2488","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, who said: We left the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and there was no bird flapping its wings in the air except that it reminded us of some knowledge from him. He said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""There remains nothing that brings one closer to Paradise and distances one from the Fire, except that it has been made clear to you."
"2489","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abi Namlah, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) when a Jewish man entered upon him and said: ""O Muhammad, does this corpse speak?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Allah knows best."" The Jew said: ""I bear witness that it speaks."" The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you, neither believe them nor reject them. But say: 'We believe in Allah, His Books, and His Messengers.' If it is true, you will not have rejected them, and if it is false, you will not have believed them."
"2490","[AI-translation] From 'Abbad ibn Shurahbil, who said: I was afflicted by a year of drought, so I entered one of the gardens of Al-Madinah. I rubbed an ear of grain and ate it, and carried some in my garment. Its owner came, struck me, and took my garment. I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said to him: ""You did not teach him when he was ignorant, nor did you feed him when he was hungry."" He then ordered him, so he returned my garment to me and gave me a wasq or half a wasq of food."
"2491","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) heard sounds and said: ""What is this?"" They said: ""They are pollinating the date-palms."" He said: ""If they were to leave it and not pollinate it, it would be better."" So they left it and did not pollinate it, and it produced inferior dates. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""What is wrong with you?"" They said: ""We left it because of what you said."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""If it is anything regarding your worldly affairs, then you are more knowledgeable of it. And if it is regarding your religion, then it is to me."
"2492","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the one who learns knowledge and then does not impart it is like the one who hoards a treasure and does not spend from it."
"2493","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Safwan ibn 'Assal al-Muradi narrated, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) while he was reclining in the mosque on a red cloak of his. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah! I have come seeking knowledge. He said: Welcome to the seeker of knowledge! Indeed, the seeker of knowledge is surrounded by angels who shade him with their wings, then they stack upon one another until they reach the lowest heaven, out of love for what he seeks. Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah! We still travel between Mecca and Medina, so give us a ruling on wiping over the leather socks? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Three days for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident."
"2494","[AI-translation] From Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Everything seeks forgiveness for the teacher of good, even the fish in the sea."
"2495","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Shimasah: That Fuqaym al-Lakhmi said to 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir: ""You go back and forth between these two targets while you are old and it is difficult for you?!"" 'Uqbah said: ""Were it not for a statement I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), I would not have endured it."" Al-Harith said: I said to Ibn Shimasah: ""And what is that?"" He said: He said: ""Whoever learns archery and then abandons it is not of us, or he has disobeyed."
"2496","[AI-translation] From 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever lies about his dream will be charged on the Day of Resurrection with tying a barley grain."
"2497","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding of the religion."
"2498","[AI-translation] From Humayd, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan delivering a sermon, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding of the religion. I am only a distributor, and Allah gives. And this Ummah will not cease to remain steadfast upon the command of Allah, not harmed by those who oppose them until the command of Allah comes."
"2499","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: Mu'awiyah rarely narrated anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), and he would say these words, rarely omitting them or narrating them on Fridays from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding of the religion. And this wealth is sweet and green. Whoever takes it with its right, it will be blessed for him. And beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter."
"2500","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""The destruction of my Ummah is in the Book and milk."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the Book and milk?"" He said: ""They learn the Quran and interpret it contrary to what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed, and they love milk, so they abandon the congregations and Friday prayers, and they take to the desert."
"2501","[AI-translation] From Nawwas bin Sam'an, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Do not argue with the Quran and do not deny the Book of Allah, part of it with part. By Allah, the believer may argue with the Quran and be defeated, and the hypocrite may argue with the Quran and defeat."
"2502","[AI-translation] From Sahl bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunayf narrating, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Do not be harsh upon yourselves, for those before you perished due to their harshness upon themselves, and you will find their remains in the hermitages and monasteries."
"2503","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The People of the Book used to read the Torah in Hebrew and interpret it in Arabic for the people of Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Neither believe the People of the Book nor disbelieve them, and say: We believe in Allah and what has been revealed to you."
"2504","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) during his Hajj on the Day of 'Arafah, while he was on his she-camel al-Qaswa', delivering a sermon, and I heard him say: ""O people! I have left among you that which, if you take hold of, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, the people of my household."
"2505","Hudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) about the good, but I used to ask him about the evil out of fear that it might reach me. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this good (and we are in it), (and He brought you), so is there any evil after this good (as there was before it)?"" (He said: ""O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,"" (three times). He said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there any good after this evil?"") He said: ""Yes."" (I said: ""Then what is the protection from it?"" He said: ""The sword."") I said: ""And is there any evil after that good?"" (And in a narration: I said: ""And is there any remainder after the sword?"") He said: ""Yes, and in it (and in a narration: there will be an emirate (and in a wording: a group) on spears, and a truce on) smoke."" I said: ""And what is its smoke?"" He said: ""A people (and in another narration: there will be after me imams (who follow other than my Sunnah, and) they guide with other than my guidance, you recognize from them and you deny (and there will arise among them men whose hearts are the hearts of devils in bodies of humans). (And in another: The truce on smoke, what is it? He said: The hearts of a people do not return to what they were upon)."" I said: ""Then is there any evil after that good?"" He said: ""Yes, (a blind and deaf fitnah upon it) are callers at the gates of Hell, whoever answers them to it they will throw him into it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said: ""They are from our skin and they speak with our tongues."" I said: ""(O Messenger of Allah!) Then what do you command me if that reaches me?"" He said: ""You adhere to the Jamāʿah of the Muslims and their Imām, (you listen and obey the Amīr even if your back is struck and your wealth is taken, so listen and obey)."" I said: ""What if they have no Jamāʿah and no Imām?"" He said: ""Then withdraw from all those sects entirely, even if you have to bite onto the root of a tree until death reaches you while you are upon that."" (And in a narration): ""So if you die, O Hudhayfah, while you are biting onto a stump, it is better for you than following any one of them."" (And in another): ""So if you see on that day Allah — Mighty and Majestic — on the earth a Caliph, then adhere to him even if your back is struck and your wealth is taken; but if you do not see a Caliph, then flee (in the earth) until death reaches you while you are biting onto the root of a tree."" (He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""Then the Dajjāl emerges."" I said: ""Then with what does he come?"" He said: ""With a river — or he said: water and fire — so whoever enters his river, his reward is nullified and his sin is obligated, and whoever enters his fire, his reward is obligated and his sin is nullified."" (I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then what is after the Dajjāl?"" He said: ""Jesus son of Mary""). He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""If you were to breed a horse, you would not ride its foal until the Hour is established."""
"2506","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen and said: ""Make things easy and do not make them difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel, and cooperate and do not differ."
